Subject: [PATCH 04351/11362] [outer-loop] KV260 terminal latency transcript
 v15: independent n=2 reproduction (live window)

Operator power-cycled the KV260 back online (2026-06-27). The terminal latency
transcript genuinely landed once before (exp3568/v14, n=1, mean 23.99us,
adversarial-clean). v1-v13 all honestly BLOCKED for months waiting for the board
to be reachable. This live window is the chance to harden the single landing to
an INDEPENDENT reproduction.

exp3600 (v15) reuses the audited v1 board harness VERBATIM (zero new attack
surface; carnot_ising_v2_n64 overlay since v4 app-registration is broken per
known-issues 2026-06-01). Captured on the live board over SSH:
  - 3000 real per-iteration UIO round-trip latencies, 251 unique values
  - mean 24.64us (v14: 23.99us -> reproduces to ~3%), p50 24.5, p99 29.47
  - same overlay + bitstream sha a90028a7..., synth_ok=true, terminal=true
  - duration 18.65s real wall-clock, live uptime captured, flagged_adversarial=None
  - adversarial_verify.py: 0 flagged, exit 0

KV260 terminal-state claim is now n=2, independently reproduced across two board
sessions. exp3568/v14 preserved (never-prune). board left with carnot_ising_v2_n64
loaded in PL (its intended Carnot-accelerator state).

